  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket that reports this exact problem. That is the Shortcut Guide log error 'Failed to copy bundled shortcut manifests ... being used by another process' on WinGet\\\\KeyboardShortcuts\\\\+WindowsNT.Notepad.en-US.yml, together with a crash when you open the PowerToys tab. Some related Shortcut Guide crashes in 0.100.x have been reported, but they have different causes. PowerToys#48170 was a missing Manifests directory (DirectoryNotFoundException). PowerToys#48773 and PowerToys#48552 are crashes when selecting the Windows tab, caused by a NullReferenceException. PowerToys#48638 is an access violation. Please file this as a new issue and include the log snippet. Check whether another process, such as a second Shortcut Guide instance, an antivirus scanner or a sync tool, has the Notepad manifest file open in %LocalAppData%\\\\Microsoft\\\\WinGet\\\\KeyboardShortcuts. A workaround to try is to close any lingering PowerToys.ShortcutGuide.exe processes and restart PowerToys. You can also disable the Shortcut Guide module until a fix is available.\"}",
